Costs.

293
00:09:55,050 --> 00:09:57,190
So which shovels last?

294
00:09:57,190 --> 00:09:58,490
Let me draw it.

295
00:09:58,490 --> 00:09:59,538
On one side,

296
00:09:59,538 --> 00:10:02,020
the shovels anyone can sell.

297
00:10:02,050 --> 00:10:02,779
Metal,

298
00:10:02,779 --> 00:10:03,507
money,

299
00:10:03,507 --> 00:10:04,520
power.

300
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:06,902
Their price rises and falls with the

301
00:10:06,902 --> 00:10:07,800
rush.

302
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:09,108
On the other side,

303
00:10:09,108 --> 00:10:11,550
the shovels nobody else can make.

304
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:12,444
The foundry,

305
00:10:12,444 --> 00:10:13,327
the machine,

306
00:10:13,327 --> 00:10:15,740
the most advanced memory.

307
00:10:15,830 --> 00:10:17,755
Those shops get to set their own

308
00:10:17,755 --> 00:10:18,630
price.

309
00:10:18,810 --> 00:10:21,430
The safest shovel isn't the biggest one.

310
00:10:21,430 --> 00:10:23,969
It's the one with no second shop.

311
00:10:24,217 --> 00:10:26,707
Hattie writes up her scorecard.

312
00:10:27,057 --> 00:10:28,975
Taiwan and the Netherlands,

313
00:10:28,975 --> 00:10:29,679
winning,

314
00:10:29,679 --> 00:10:32,107
as long as nobody builds a second

315
00:10:32,107 --> 00:10:34,407
shop and politics stays calm.

316
00:10:34,767 --> 00:10:35,756
South Korea,

317
00:10:35,756 --> 00:10:36,745
winning big,

318
00:10:36,745 --> 00:10:38,867
on a rollercoaster.

319
00:10:39,127 --> 00:10:40,020
Japan,

320
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:42,777
steady and hard to replace.

321
00:10:43,027 --> 00:10:43,717
The Gulf,

322
00:10:43,717 --> 00:10:46,457
buying a seat at every table.

323
00:10:46,637 --> 00:10:48,212
Chile and Australia,

324
00:10:48,212 --> 00:10:49,558
rich in the good years,

325
00:10:49,558 --> 00:10:51,984
exposed in the bad ones.

326
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:54,335
So can a country win the AI

327
00:10:54,335 --> 00:10:57,280
economy without building AI?

328
00:10:57,430 --> 00:10:58,290
Yes.

329
00:10:58,290 --> 00:10:59,970
Some already are.

330
00:11:00,050 --> 00:11:01,881
But the winners aren't the ones who

331
00:11:01,881 --> 00:11:03,030
dig the most.

332
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:05,099
They're the ones who own a shovel

333
00:11:05,099 --> 00:11:06,600
nobody can copy,

334
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,776
and keep inventing the next one before

335
00:11:08,776 --> 00:11:10,465
the rush moves on.

336
00:11:10,717 --> 00:11:11,599
Back home,

337
00:11:11,599 --> 00:11:14,837
Hattie repaints the sign above her door.

338
00:11:14,837 --> 00:11:16,867
Nugget hops onto the counter.

339
00:11:16,897 --> 00:11:18,607
So what do we sell now?

340
00:11:18,767 --> 00:11:20,287
Hattie smiles.

341
00:11:20,287 --> 00:11:23,192
Whatever they can't get anywhere else.

342
00:11:23,450 --> 00:11:24,070
Next time,

343
00:11:24,070 --> 00:11:26,850
we follow the money behind another hidden

344
00:11:26,850 --> 00:11:29,160
link of the world economy.

345
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:31,339
This is The Hidden Economics.
